[36m(TaskRunner pid=1063442)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1063442)[0m To solve this, we can use the concept of Fermat's point for polygons. Fermat's point (also known as the Torricelli point) minimizes the sum of the distances to the vertices of a triangle. We will extend this idea to a pentagon by breaking it down into smaller components.
